<p>Decimal 36878. Default value: 0. Also known as <strong>VICCRE</strong>.</p>
<p>Sound volume and auxiliary colour, packed into one byte.</p>

<p><strong>Bits 7-4</strong> - auxiliary colour. This is the fourth colour available to
multicolour characters, selected by the bit pair 11 in the character data, and it
is shared by every multicolour character on the screen. All 16 colours can be
used:</p>
<ul>
<li>Black - 0</li>
<li>White - 1</li>
<li>Red - 2</li>
<li>Cyan - 3</li>
<li>Purple - 4</li>
<li>Green - 5</li>
<li>Blue - 6</li>
<li>Yellow - 7</li>
<li>Orange - 8</li>
<li>Lt Orange - 9</li>
<li>Pink - 10</li>
<li>Lt Cyan - 11</li>
<li>Lt Purple - 12</li>
<li>Lt Green - 13</li>
<li>Lt Blue - 14</li>
<li>Lt Yellow - 15</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Bits 3-0</strong> - master sound volume, 0 for silence and 15 for full volume.
This is a single volume for all four voices; the VIC 20 has no per voice
volume.</p>

<p>Because the two live in the same register, write them together:</p>
<code>
// full volume, pink (10) as the multicolour auxiliary colour
AUX_COLOR_AND_VOLUME := (10 * 16) + 15;

// full volume, auxiliary colour left as black
AUX_COLOR_AND_VOLUME := 15;
</code>
<p>See also SOUND1_REGISTER through SOUNDFX_REGISTER for the voices themselves.</p>
